  "context_markdown": "This public register records known, intentional differences between the supplied printed source and the present working edition. The choices listed here are adopted now; they do not establish the original transcribers’ intentions. Entries follow score order.\n\nAll 37 supplied source pages and all 31 incoming native engraving pages were compared across the four staves, followed by magnified checks of candidates. The supplied scan is the Rózsavölgyi first edition, catalogued 1911, reprinted by Boosey & Hawkes. This is a source comparison, not a fresh exhaustive note-by-note transcription, a collation of all historical witnesses or a guarantee that every small mark has been individually verified.\n\nMovement III has separately numbered **Introduzione** and **Allegro vivace** sections. The main Allegro’s standalone quarter-rest bar after 264 is source 265, labelled X1 in this edition. Thereafter source numbers are one higher than edition numbers until the source’s final system on PDF p.36 repeats 350 after a six-bar system beginning 349. From that system to the end, edition numbers are four higher than source numbers. The final source 375 is edition 379. Wherever numbers differ, entries show both; ordering follows physical score position, not the repeated printed numbers.",
